## Rule 1: SDK Version & Manifest

- Always use `"sdk": 3` in app.json for new apps
- Set `"compatibility": ">=5.0.0"` minimum
- Use semantic versioning for `"version"` (e.g., "1.0.0")
- Pre-release versions (1.0.0-beta) are NOT allowed in App Store

```json
{
  "id": "com.example.myapp",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "compatibility": ">=5.0.0",
  "sdk": 3,
  "platforms": ["local"]
}
```

## Rule 2: Async/Await Pattern

- SDK v3 uses promises exclusively - NO callbacks
- All lifecycle methods are async
- Always use try/catch for error handling

```javascript
// CORRECT
async onInit() {
  try {
    await this.initializeDevice();
  } catch (error) {
    this.error('Failed to initialize:', error);
  }
}

// WRONG - Don't use callbacks
onInit(callback) {
  this.initializeDevice((err) => {
    callback(err);
  });
}
```

## Rule 3: Homey API Access

- Access all managers through `this.homey`
- Never import managers directly

```javascript
// CORRECT
this.homey.settings.get('key');
this.homey.flow.getActionCard('id');
this.homey.api.devices.getDevices();

// WRONG
const ManagerSettings = require('homey').ManagerSettings;
```

## Rule 4: Device Capabilities

- Register capability listeners in `onInit()`
- Use `setCapabilityValue()` to update state
- Handle unavailable devices gracefully

```javascript
async onInit() {
  this.registerCapabilityListener('onoff', async (value) => {
    await this.sendCommand(value);
  });
}

async poll() {
  try {
    const status = await this.fetchStatus();
    await this.setCapabilityValue('onoff', status.isOn);
    await this.setAvailable();
  } catch (error) {
    await this.setUnavailable('Device offline');
  }
}
```

## Rule 5: Permissions

- Only request permissions you need
- Some permissions block Homey Cloud deployment
- Check platform before using local-only features

```javascript
// Check platform
if (this.homey.platform === 'local') {
  // Use local-only features (Web API, LED ring, etc.)
}
```

### Permissions Blocking Cloud:
- `homey:manager:api`
- `homey:manager:ledring`
- `homey:wireless:*`

## Rule 6: Persistent Storage

| Use Case | Method |
|----------|--------|
| App settings | `this.homey.settings.get/set()` |
| Device credentials | `this.getStoreValue/setStoreValue()` |
| User preferences | Device settings (in manifest) |
| Large/binary files | Userdata folder |

```javascript
// App settings
this.homey.settings.set('apiKey', key);

// Device store (persists across restarts)
await this.setStoreValue('token', accessToken);
const token = this.getStoreValue('token');
```

## Rule 7: Flow Cards

- Define in app.json or `.homeycompose/flow/`
- Register run listeners in `onInit()`
- Use `titleFormatted` with `[[arg]]` placeholders

```javascript
async onInit() {
  const action = this.homey.flow.getActionCard('my_action');
  action.registerRunListener(async (args) => {
    await this.performAction(args.value);
  });
}
```

## Rule 8: Driver Pairing

- Return devices with unique `data.id`
- Include discovery logic in `onPairListDevices()`

```javascript
async onPairListDevices() {
  const discovered = await this.discover();
  return discovered.map(d => ({
    name: d.name,
    data: { id: d.uniqueId },
    settings: { ip: d.ip }
  }));
}
```

## Rule 9: Error Handling

- Use `this.log()` for info, `this.error()` for errors
- Throw user-friendly errors in flow cards
- Set device unavailable on connection errors

```javascript
async onCapability(value) {
  try {
    await this.sendCommand(value);
  } catch (error) {
    this.error('Command failed:', error);
    throw new Error('Could not reach device');
  }
}
```

## Rule 10: Widgets (Homey Pro only)

- Requires `"compatibility": ">=12.3.0"`
- Only on `"platforms": ["local"]`
- Use CSS variables for theming
- Call `Homey.ready()` when initialized

## Rule 11: Web API (Homey Pro only)

- Define endpoints in app.json `api` section
- Implement handlers in `api.js`
- Keep endpoints private by default

## Rule 12: Wireless Protocols

| Protocol | Permission | Package |
|----------|------------|---------|
| Wi-Fi | none | Native HTTP |
| Zigbee | `homey:wireless:zigbee` | `homey-zigbeedriver` |
| Z-Wave | `homey:wireless:zwave` | `homey-zwavedriver` |
| BLE | `homey:wireless:ble` | Native BLE |
| 433 MHz | `homey:wireless:433` | Native RF |
| IR | `homey:wireless:ir` | Native IR |
| Matter | none | Native Matter |

